# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in every working
# tree on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The Autotools inputs (configure.ac, Makefile.am) are
# processed by m4, and a CRLF checkout turns each line continuation into
# "\" followed by CR, which is not a continuation at all. The generated
# configure then contains broken "for x in \" lists and dies at run time
# with "syntax error near unexpected token". Pinning eol=lf keeps the
# generated script valid everywhere, including Windows/MSYS2 where the
# system git default is core.autocrlf=true.
#
# Keeping the index and the working tree at LF also means a clone on one
# platform does not look modified on another.
* text=auto eol=lf

# EPS is PostScript text, and the repository copy is LF. It is listed
# explicitly so the "binary" rules below cannot silently stop normalizing it
# and commit a CRLF blob.
*.eps text eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.odt binary
*.odp binary
*.sixel binary
